<title>INDIA: India's Sterlite 6-mth to December 1996 up 2.7 pct.</title>
<headline>India's Sterlite 6-mth to December 1996 up 2.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-months to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  705.3    vs     686.8</p>
<p>    Net sales		 4,267.4    vs   4,049.3</p>
<p>    Other income		153.6    vs     147.9</p>
<p>    Expenditure	     3,534.9    vs   3,358.1</p>
<p>    Interest		     56.2    vs	70.9</p>
<p>    Gross profit		829.9    vs     768.2</p>
<p>    Depreciation		114.6    vs	80.3</p>
<p>    Tax			    10.0    vs	1.10</p>
<p>Note: Sterlite Industries, a major cable manufacturer, said it expected better second half performance with higher sales of Jelly Filled Telecom Cables (JFTC) and from its copper smelter project.</p>
<p>It said the despatches of JFTC were &quot;considerably&quot; lower during the period ending December 1996 due to a delay in getting orders from the Department of Telecommunications.</p>
<p>Sterlite said it had decided to &quot;hive off a project for manufacture of 60,000 tpa writing and printing paper to be implemented in a separate company.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
